0..75 Comment "// Grade algebras as models of `std.grade`\'s `Grade`, each order decided by"
76..90 Comment "// conversion."
91..93 Comment "//"
94..165 Comment "// `Usage` orders the grades the tree writes, and `Count` counts in the"
166..241 Comment "// prelude\'s binary naturals. A path from an order to `true` checks exactly"
242..316 Comment "// when the order holds, so `gandr check` settles whether one grade covers"
317..328 Comment "// another."
329..331 Comment "//"
332..405 Comment "// The checker evaluates each order over closed constructor data, and the"
406..478 Comment "// kernel replays the conversion. A numeral annotated `(n : Nat)` is its"
479..557 Comment "// constructor term, so a quantity in gibibytes compares in a few dozen steps."
558..560 Comment "//"
561..640 Comment "// - see: `../../../library/std/src/grade.gandr` — `Grade`, `Usage`, `Count`,"
641..672 Comment "//   `Hom`, `fits` and `covers`"
673..749 Comment "// - see: `../../pathological/effects/grade-algebra.gandr` — an order that"
750..813 Comment "//   does not hold, and one the native integers leave undecided"
814..872 Comment "// - see: #3287 — grade algebras as models of one theory"
874..935 Comment "// The grade theory, its two models and the map between them."
